---
import CommercialLayout from '../../components/CommercialLayout.astro';
import CitabilityBlock from '../../components/CitabilityBlock.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const utm = Astro.url.searchParams.get('utm') || 'audit-page';
const canonical = `${SITE.url}/audit/`;

const FAQ = [
  {
    question: 'Is the assessment free?',
    answer:
      'Yes. You send the form, we reply in writing within two working days: which module moves your number, a fixed price for it, and, if the honest answer is that nothing we sell would help, that answer. No obligation either way.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What do you need from us?',
    answer:
      'The site address, a few lines about how inbound works today (site, forms, chat, CRM, who follows up), and the number you want to move. Screenshots help; access to production systems is never needed at this stage.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is there a call?',
    answer:
      'Not at this stage: everything is in writing, so you can read it when it suits you and forward it to whoever decides. A working call is part of fix packages and setups from 1,000 USD.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What do I get back?',
    answer:
      'A written reply with the gap we see, the module that addresses it, what it costs and what it does not cover. Paid work is quoted with a fixed scope and a fixed price; nothing starts without your yes.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What if the answer is that we do not need you?',
    answer:
      'Then we say so. If the fix is a setting in software you already pay for, we name the setting. If your funnel converts fine and the constraint is traffic, no automation changes that arithmetic and you should know it early.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can we check the site ourselves first?',
    answer:
      'Yes. The free AI visibility check scores any site in ten seconds, and the inbound lead audit guide publishes the full method, so you can reconcile your own numbers before writing to us.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: FAQ.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.answer },
  })),
};
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Free Written Assessment: Where Your Inbound Leaks · OperStack"
  description="Send your site and how inbound works today; get a written reply within two working days: the gap we see, the module that fixes it, a fixed price. No call, no obligation."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={faqSchema}
>
  <div class="wrap audit-wrap">
    <h1>Free written assessment</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Send your site and a few lines about how inbound works today. Within two working days you
      get a written reply: where leads leak, which module fixes it, and a fixed price. No call,
      no deck, no obligation, and you keep the reply either way.
    </p>

    <CitabilityBlock
      text="OperStack's assessment is free and in writing: you describe your site and inbound process, and within two working days you receive the gap we see, the module that addresses it and a fixed price for it."
    />

    <h2>The four counts</h2>
    <p>
      Almost every inbound problem shows up as a gap between two of these. Teams usually know one
      of the numbers and assume the other three. If you have them, put them in the form; if not,
      the <a href="/guides/inbound-lead-audit/">inbound lead audit guide</a> shows how to get them
      from your own systems in an afternoon.
    </p>
    <ol class="numbers">
      <li><b>Arrived.</b> Requests submitted across every channel, including the ones that never reached a system.</li>
      <li><b>Created.</b> Records that exist in the CRM. The gap to arrived is a capture or integration failure.</li>
      <li><b>Owned.</b> Records with a live, correct owner. The gap here is almost always a routing rule with no fallback branch.</li>
      <li><b>Worked.</b> Records that received a real first response. The gap is coverage, capacity, or a queue nobody watches.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>A written reply within two working days, not a meeting invitation</li>
      <li>The gap we see from what you sent, traced to one layer: capture, routing, follow-up or reporting</li>
      <li>The module that addresses it, with a fixed price and an explicit list of what it does not cover</li>
      <li>A build, buy, or configure verdict, including when the answer is a setting you already own</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we need from you</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>The site address and the market you sell in</li>
      <li>A few lines on how inbound works today: forms, chat, CRM, who follows up and how fast</li>
      <li>The number you want to move, and the four counts above if you have them</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      We do not ask for access to production systems, and you should be sceptical of anyone
      who does at this stage. Want an instant reading first? The
      <a href="/ai-visibility/">free AI visibility check</a> scores any site in ten seconds.
    </p>

    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <p>
      Not a maturity score. Scoring an organisation from one to five creates a gap and positions
      the scorer to fill it. Not a vendor shortlist either: we take no commission from any tool,
      which is why a recommendation is sometimes to change a setting rather than buy anything.
      And not a call: a working session is part of fix packages and setups from 1,000 USD.
    </p>

    <h2>After the assessment</h2>
    <p>
      If something is worth building, it is quoted per module against
      <a href="/services/">the services</a> and priced on
      <a href="/pricing/">the pricing page</a>. The most common outcomes are
      <a href="/services/lead-routing-software/">lead routing setup</a>,
      <a href="/services/ai-automation-services/">AI automation services</a>, and
      <a href="/services/lead-management-system/">lead management system setup</a>.
      For search and AI visibility there is the written
      <a href="/products/seo-audit/">SEO, AEO and GEO audit</a> with a price on the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Send the request</h2>

    <form id="audit-form" novalidate>
      <input type="hidden" name="source" value={`audit:${utm}`} />
      <div class="row">
        <div>
          <label for="name">Name *</label>
          <input id="name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="phone">WhatsApp / Phone *</label>
          <input id="phone" name="phone" type="tel" required autocomplete="tel" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="email">Email</label>
        <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="message">What does your inbound look like today?</label>
        <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" placeholder="Site, CRM, team size, market..."></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="consent">
        <input type="checkbox" id="consent" name="consent" required />
        <label for="consent">I agree to be contacted about this request.</label>
      </div>
      <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label for="website">Website</label>
        <input id="website" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn" id="submit">Send the request →</button>
      <p class="msg" id="form-msg" hidden></p>
    </form>

    <FaqSection items={FAQ} />
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ utm }}>
    const form = document.getElementById('audit-form');
    const msg = document.getElementById('form-msg');
    const btn = document.getElementById('submit');
    const loadedAt = Date.now();

    /* Funnel step between page view and submit: how many visitors actually start
       filling the form. Fires once, on the first real input rather than on focus,
       because focus also fires when someone just tabs through the page. */
    let started = false;
    const markStart = () => {
      if (started) return;
      started = true;
      if (typeof window.operStackTrack === 'function') {
        window.operStackTrack('lead_form_start', { form_name: 'audit', source: `audit:${utm}` });
      }
    };
    form.addEventListener('input', markStart, { once: true });
    form.addEventListener('change', markStart, { once: true });

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      msg.hidden = true;
      btn.disabled = true;
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      const payload = {
        name: fd.get('name'),
        phone: fd.get('phone'),
        email: fd.get('email'),
        message: fd.get('message'),
        source: fd.get('source') || `audit:${utm}`,
        website: fd.get('website'),
        formLoadedAt: loadedAt,
        formElapsedMs: Date.now() - loadedAt,
      };
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/lead/', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.error || 'Request failed');
        if (typeof window.operStackTrack === 'function') {
          window.operStackTrack('lead_form_submit', { form_name: 'audit', source: payload.source });
        }
        window.location.href = '/thanks/';
      } catch (err) {
        msg.textContent = err.message || 'Something went wrong. Email info@oper-stack.com';
        msg.className = 'msg err';
        msg.hidden = false;
        btn.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  </script>
</CommercialLayout>

<style>
  .audit-wrap { max-width: 720px; }
  .bullets { margin: 0 0 24px 20px; color: var(--muted); }
  .bullets li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .pricing-link {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  form {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 28px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(61, 184, 169, 0.22);
  }
  label { display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; color: rgba(245, 242, 236, 0.9); }
  input, textarea {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
    color: var(--paper);
    font: inherit;
  }
  input:focus, textarea:focus {
    outline: 2px solid rgba(61, 184, 169, 0.45);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  .row { display: grid; gap: 16px; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; opacity: 0; height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .msg { font-size: 14px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .msg.err { color: #f5a962; }
  .consent { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .consent input { width: auto; margin-top: 3px; }
</style>
